  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_7' aria-label=\" Milind S/o Ashruba Dhanve and Ors. versus The State of Maharashtra pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('7','2026','2026_4_565_592','2026INSC355'); ><font size='4'> <strong>MILIND S/O ASHRUBA DHANVE AND ORS.<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>THE STATE OF MAHARASHTRA </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 4 S.C.R. 565</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 355</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001292026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : J.K. MAHESHWARI<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup></strong><br> Issue for Consideration Whether the Appellants are entitled to the benefit of ss.3 and 4 of the Probation of Offenders Act, 1958, and if so, to what extent; whether the benefit of s.4 of the 1958 Act is available to an offender who has been sentenced only with payment of fine, and not imprisonment. Headnotes&dagger; Probation of Offenders Act, 1958 &ndash; ss.3, 4 &ndash; Power of court to release certain offenders after admonition or on probation of good conduct &ndash; Penal Code, 1860 &ndash; s.53 &ndash; Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), 2023 &ndash; s.4 &ndash; Benefit of<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 10-04-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CRIMINAL APPEAL No. 1893/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Disposed off</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('7','2026','2026_4_565_592','2026INSC355','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='c